    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0121" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg37"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bryan to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-11-07"><hi rendition="#italic">November 7,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 466.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Continuing the subject of my No. 464, of
                    October 31, I have the honor to report that the French minister informs me that
                    the legal adviser of the foreign office at Paris, in a lengthy opinion, has
                    sustained his position regarding the illegality of the imposition of duties on
                    merchandise in transit by the Amazon.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Page
                    Bryan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
